Template: rockchip-vaapi/configure-environment
Type: boolean
Default: true
Description: Set the VA-API environment variables for Firefox system-wide?
 This package can install environment settings so that Firefox uses the
 Rockchip hardware video decoder without setting variables by hand in every
 session.
 .
 Files written:
   /etc/profile.d/rockchip-vaapi.sh            (terminal sessions)
   /etc/environment.d/60-rockchip-vaapi.conf   (desktop sessions)
 .
 Variables set:
   LIBVA_DRIVER_NAME=rockchip
   LIBVA_DRIVERS_PATH=/usr/lib/aarch64-linux-gnu/dri
   MOZ_DISABLE_RDD_SANDBOX=1
   MOZ_ENABLE_WAYLAND=1
   MOZ_X11_EGL=1
 .
 MOZ_DISABLE_RDD_SANDBOX=1 turns off the sandbox of Firefox's media decoding
 process, for every user of this machine.
 .
 Log out and back in for the change to take effect. To change the answer
 later, run: dpkg-reconfigure rockchip-vaapi
